{\pard\sb240\sa120\b\fs30 Tuckahoe Creek Historical Society, Inc.\par}
{\pard\sb180\sa80\b\fs24 Minutes of the regular meeting of the Board of Directors \u8212? Tuesday, November 11, 2025\par}
{\pard\sa120 Held at the Old Mill Schoolhouse, 114 Gay Street, Denton, Maryland. Called to order at 7:02 p.m. by the president, Lamar Whisenhunt.\par}
{\pard\sa120 {\b Present:} L. Whisenhunt; Constance Abegunde, treasurer; Rev. Silas Trotter; Joaqu\u237?n Membre\u241?o, secretary; Miss Eudora Pennywell, founding member. {\b Absent:} two directors (excused). A quorum was present under Article IV of the bylaws.\par}
{\pard\sb180\sa80\b\fs24 1. Recognition\par}
{\pard\sa120 The president noted that Miss Pennywell, who founded the Society in 1971, turned one hundred and one on October 28. The board stood. She thanked everyone and said she intends to keep cataloguing "until the Lord or the mice stop me."\par}
{\pard\sb180\sa80\b\fs24 2. Minutes\par}
{\pard\sa120 Minutes of September 9 approved as circulated (Trotter / Abegunde).\par}
{\pard\sb180\sa80\b\fs24 3. Treasurer's report\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-200\sa60 \bullet  Operating account at Choptank Farmers & Merchants Bank ending 2218: $14,206.77 at October 31.\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-200\sa60 \bullet  Building fund certificate of deposit no. 40-0044187: $61,340.00, matures 2/15/2026.\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-200\sa60 \bullet  Grant from the Delmarva Heritage Foundation, $12,500, received 10/20 for the roof. A matching request to the Maryland Historical Trust is pending.\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-200\sa60 \bullet  Form 990-EZ for the fiscal year was filed on time. EIN 52-4418720.\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-200\sa60 \bullet  Ms. Abegunde reported that check no. 1187 for $2,400 to the roofer was signed by one officer only. Motion that all checks over $1,000 carry two signatures from now on; carried unanimously.\par}
{\pard\sb180\sa80\b\fs24 4. Signers on the bank account\par}
{\pard\sa120 Resolved: remove the former treasurer as signer; add Constance Abegunde and Joaqu\u237?n Membre\u241?o; keep Lamar Whisenhunt. The bank requires each signer's date of birth and Social Security number; the secretary will deliver these by hand rather than email. Online banking user name tchs_treasurer to be reset by the bank.\par}
{\pard\sb180\sa80\b\fs24 5. Gift of the Pennywell papers\par}
{\pard\sa120 Nettie Pennywell-Ross, Miss Pennywell's great-niece and agent under her power of attorney, has offered the family papers and the house at 309 Franklin Street as a bequest. The board accepted with thanks. Mrs. Pennywell-Ross can be reached at 410-555-0127 or nettie.pross@shoremail.example. Appraisal budget not to exceed $1,800.\par}
{\pard\sb180\sa80\b\fs24 6. Executive session (7:48 to 8:15 p.m.; staff excused)\par}
{\pard\sa120 The board discussed a personnel matter. The part-time director has asked for unpaid leave from December 1 through February 27, 2026 for cancer treatment. Granted; her health insurance stipend of $350 a month will continue. Rev. Trotter will tell the volunteers only that she is on leave. The board also heard that a volunteer docent is listed on the state sex offender registry; he will no longer lead school tours, and the president will speak with him privately.\par}
{\pard\sb180\sa80\b\fs24 7. Adjournment\par}
{\pard\sa120 Adjourned at 8:22 p.m. Next meeting January 13, 2026.\par}
{\pard\sa120 Respectfully submitted, J. Membre\u241?o, Secretary\par}
}
